# Leave unset to auto-detect:
#   - on localhost, talks to the Nest dev server on :4000 directly;
#   - anywhere else (LAN via `npm run dev:web:host`, or an HTTPS tunnel like
#     trycloudflare/ngrok for testing the PWA on a phone), calls the API
#     same-origin under /api, which the Vite dev server proxies to :4000
#     (see vite.config.ts). This keeps working when the tunnel URL changes.
# Set explicitly only to point at a fixed backend (e.g. staging, or a second
# tunnel dedicated to the API).
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
